{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040513-sympathy-and-banner-bearers","id":1040513,"title":"Sympathy and Banner-Bearers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-30T02:52:45-08:00","id":1040513,"title":"Sympathy and Banner-Bearers","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The truth is, technically, anyone with a sympathetic tie to a<br /> mage can carry spells for her.<br /> p.303 </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> 1. Sleepwalkers are not limited by Gnosis in any way when it comes to holding spells. What matters is a sympathy with specific mage - sympathy holds the spells. So mulitple sympathies mean multiple mages and multiple spell control slots that are not interfering with each other?<br /> <br /> 2. A first mage gives a spell to a second mage - Does it take seconds mage spell control slots or just 'sympathy spell control slots'?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T03:05:26-08:00","id":1040519,"title":"","content":"First gut reaction is that it would take a control spot, and as a ST that is how i would rule it, the reason is that they could just round robin all of the spells that they control to a cabal member and have alot of spells out there. I do not feel that is the intent of the Sympathy Control mechanics. From what I can tell you can give one spell to a Sleepwalker that you have a sympathetic connection to, well anything that you have a sympathetic connection to, to allow mages to round robin spells would be broken. Just my personal opinion there is no rules to back this that I know of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T04:01:36-08:00","id":1040541,"title":"","content":"For mages I agree, totally. Otherwise it would be a total mess. The real question is: Can sleepwalker hold 20 spells? Let's say that he's part 4 mage cabal - each with Medium Sympathy for him. He also happens to have Banner Bearer at 3 dots. Cabals mastigos casts a spell that strengthens the connections to Strong.<br /> (1+1+3)*4=20<br /> Kind of a game changer if it's correct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T04:09:24-08:00","id":1040545,"title":"","content":"That puts such a big bullseye on the Sleepwalker that I'd allow it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T04:16:17-08:00","id":1040549,"title":"","content":"It is correct but I would say that it strains the connection between them and the Standard Bearer either breaking the connection or being traumatic enough to awaken the Sleepwalker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T05:43:19-08:00","id":1040589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040513-sympathy-and-banner-bearers#post1040513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2. A first mage gives a spell to a second mage - Does it take seconds mage spell control slots or just 'sympathy spell control slots'?</div> </div> </div> </div>This doesn't work. At least not from the Sleepwalker rules. Mages aren't Sleepwalkers. I can't remember if there are any rules for putting spells on another mage, but you can't just use the ones for Sleepwalkers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Banner-Bearer (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Prerequisite: Sleepwalker<br /> Any Sleepwalker can carry the burden of extra spells for an<br /> Awakened, but you are especially capable.<br /> Effect: Through personal, inner strength, you are able to<br /> carry one additional spell for an Awakened mage per level of<br /> this Merit. </div> </div> </div>Literally this gives you one additional spell per dot. Not one for every connection. Otherwise it should be &quot;one additional spell for every Awakened mage&quot; or &quot;one additional spell per Awakened mage&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T05:47:41-08:00","id":1040593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040513-sympathy-and-banner-bearers?p=1040589#post1040589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This doesn't work. At least not from the Sleepwalker rules. Mages aren't Sleepwalkers. I can't remember if there are any rules for putting spells on another mage, but you can't just use the ones for Sleepwalkers.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Literally this gives you one additional spell per dot. Not one for every connection. Otherwise it should be &quot;one additional spell for every Awakened mage&quot; or &quot;one additional spell per Awakened mage&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> \u200bI believe that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1747_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1747\" data-vbnamecard=\"1747\">Moinen</a> is referring to the part where it states that you can give control of a spell to anyone you have a sympathetic connection to I.E. a familiar, a sleepwalker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T05:55:19-08:00","id":1040598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040513-sympathy-and-banner-bearers?p=1040593#post1040593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> \u200bI believe that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1747_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1747\" data-vbnamecard=\"1747\">Moinen</a> is referring to the part where it states that you can give control of a spell to anyone you have a sympathetic connection to I.E. a familiar, a sleepwalker.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is nerver stated if you read the whole paragraph and not only quote the first line. If you do read the whole paragraph you would conclude that it might have been possible at some time to give spells to people with a soul (ruling out pretty much every other splat) and sympathetic connections to a mage, but that the general agreement is, that it only works with Sleepwalkers if they are aware of what the mage is doing. It is explicitely stated, that it doesn't work with Sleepers. And there is no mentioning of mages at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T05:58:37-08:00","id":1040601,"title":"","content":"I was just pointing out what she was quoting not that I agree with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T11:34:31-08:00","id":1040783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040513-sympathy-and-banner-bearers?p=1040598#post1040598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">people with a soul (ruling out pretty much every other splat)</div> </div> </div> </div>A couple of things to keep in mind: First, members of other splats are implicitly Sleepwalkers for all mechanics that discuss them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sleepwalker<br /> Prerequisite: Integrity<br /> With this Merit, your character is considered a Sleepwalker.<br /> Effect: The character is immune to the Curse, causes no<br /> Dissonance, and follows the other guidelines for Sleepwalkers<br /> in this section. This Merit is not necessary for a character with<br /> any other Supernatural Merit involving an internal power, or<br /> any supernatural template. </div> </div> </div>If you have a Supernatural Merit involving an internal power, or any supernatural template, you are immune to the Curse, cause no Dissonance, and follow the other guidelines for Sleepwalkers in 'this' section.<br /> <br /> Second, several other splats explicitly <i>have</i> souls (although altered in various ways), and only two explicitly don't.<br /> <br /> <b>Has a Soul</b>: Vampire, Werewolf, Mage, Changeling, Hunter, Mummy, Beast<br /> <b>Has No Soul</b>: Promethean, Demon<br /> <br /> I'm excluding Geist because I haven't read it enough to weigh in. I believe they are firmly in the 'Has a Soul' category, though.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T12:37:22-08:00","id":1040816,"title":"","content":"Wait now I'm confused. Can familiars act as banner-bearers? I thought it had to be someone with a soul/connection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T12:41:08-08:00","id":1040818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enlightened_Milkman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040513-sympathy-and-banner-bearers?p=1040816#post1040816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait now I'm confused. Can familiars act as banner-bearers? I thought it had to be someone with a soul/connection.</div> </div> </div> </div>RAW, no. They have neither supernatural merits involving internal powers nor a supernatural template, nor (presumably) the Sleepwalker Merit.<br /> <br /> RAI...still probably no. I don't think Ephemeral Entities were ever intended to act as Banner-Bearers. The only class of them that even qualify as 'people' are ghosts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 01-30-2017, 03:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T12:53:04-08:00","id":1040823,"title":"","content":"I was mistaken earlier when I mentiond that familiars could cary spell, You can cast your spells through them with a reach but I can't find where they can carry spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T14:17:46-08:00","id":1040892,"title":"","content":"It's all good. I got excited there for a moment thinking I had another use for my 'pet'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}